\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{An alternating covector gives an ordered field polynomial}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{At one vertex, the [paired matter algebra](fdip-00TJ)
contains the ordered unbarred word
#{\psi_{x,1}\psi_{x,2}} and the word with the opposite
order. The two are related by the exterior-algebra sign
rule. An alternating bilinear form also has coefficients
for both orders. How can such a form determine a
gauge-invariant matter insertion over rings where
two has no inverse?}
